; A top-level rule whose entire body is a TAG-WRAPPED bare fixed value (`#6.5(5)`). The tag is
; irrelevant to the gap: unwrapping the single-type tag head lands on the same bare `Fixed` inner as
; `foo = 5`, which has no standalone Rust representation (a `Fixed` only ever exists as an unstored
; struct/array member), so generation used to panic in `for_rust_member`/`for_wasm_member`. It is now
; rejected GRACEFULLY at rule registration (`intermediate::register_type_alias`) via the normal
; rejection channel, surfaced as an `Err` at `finalize` — hence `error (graceful)` in the catalog.
;
; The bare (untagged) variants of this same gap are pinned as matrix rows (`value.number`,
; `value.text`, `type2.value`, `prelude.true`/`false`/`nil`/`null`), projected into
; `tests/matrix_reject/`; this hand fixture pins the tag-wrapped shape, which no matrix row covers.
; Supporting these (a wrapper newtype carrying the constant) is future work. The auto-wrapping
; tag-inner variants that ARE supported carry a `.default` or a range on the inner (pinned by
; `tests/corpus/tagged_default_inner.cddl` / `tagged_ranged_inner.cddl`) — those resolve to a
; primitive wrapper, not a bare `Fixed`, so they stay untouched.
tagged = #6.5(5)
